      "invariant": "INV-MCVSM81V",
      "origin": {
        "leaf": "260921-ICR-L48"
      },
      "rationale": "Its `selectSubject` records, in the focus request it leaves, the element that had focus when the reader made the selection.",
      "role": "support"
    },
    {
      "anchor": {
        "blob": "7c6601ddf7269a084e197eb6ae1f071a8c3acef6",
        "content": "sha256:2bea560c5f336151a88c4c7f72860d44ec8070841375b4f546fdeee71624801b",
        "locator": {
          "kind": "symbol",
          "name": "useRefreshReview"
        }
      },
      "id": "RLZ-BDCHZ3",
      "invariant": "INV-T1ZHP5",
      "origin": {
        "handoffEntry": "MIK-R39@v1-focus-request-answered-by-its-selection",
        "leaf": "260928-MIK-L39"
      },
      "rationale": "Its `refreshReview` leaves a request that only scrolls and remembers the read on screen at the click. Its `settle` drops that request when the read on screen is failed or refused and is not the one remembered, and remembers that read as the refresh's failure. Its `retryReview` settles first and then is the refresh again when the read on screen is that failure; otherwise it only reads again. The cases \"forgets the scroll a refresh asked for when its read fails, so a later page of the subject leaves the rail alone\", \"brings the selected row into view after a refresh asked in the turn that shows a failed read\" and \"brings the selected row into view when the retry is made in the turn that shows the failed refresh\" of `dashboard/src/panels/review/ReviewSurface.walkFresh.test.tsx` test these three paths.",
      "role": "primary-authority"
    },
    {
      "anchor": {
        "blob": "7c6601ddf7269a084e197eb6ae1f071a8c3acef6",
        "content": "sha256:2bea560c5f336151a88c4c7f72860d44ec8070841375b4f546fdeee71624801b",
        "locator": {
          "kind": "symbol",
          "name": "useRefreshReview"
        }
      },
      "id": "RLZ-FRKWFP",
      "invariant": "INV-9ZKYWQ",
      "origin": {
        "handoffEntry": "MIK-R39@v1-other-selections-start-afresh",
        "leaf": "260928-MIK-L39"
      },
      "rationale": "Its `refreshReview` begins a selection that does not keep before it asks the read cycle to read again, so a refresh shows the comparison as it reads now and not the tree walked before it. The case \"starts afresh at a refresh of the review\" of `dashboard/src/panels/review/ReviewSurface.walkFresh.test.tsx` tests it.",
      "role": "enforcement"
    },
    {
      "anchor": {
        "blob": "7c6601ddf7269a084e197eb6ae1f071a8c3acef6",
        "content": "sha256:a4cb15f991923645d5bd6bd9654729ebd68da71c047ec096d8112ba5087c5a36",
        "locator": {
          "kind": "symbol",
          "name": "subjectSelection"
        }
      },
      "id": "RLZ-KQQ22F",
      "invariant": "INV-9ZKYWQ",
      "origin": {
        "handoffEntry": "MIK-R39@v1-other-selections-start-afresh",
        "leaf": "260928-MIK-L39"
      },
      "rationale": "Its `selectSubject` is the one handler of every subject selection and begins it with the tree intent `keep` only when the options say so; every other selection begins with `keep` false. Its `openTaskContext`, the offer after a refusal, begins a selection that does not keep. The cases \"starts afresh at \"All source changes\"\" and \"keeps every row when a selected subject is refused, and starts afresh at the offer of the task context\" of `dashboard/src/panels/review/ReviewSurface.walkFresh.test.tsx` test two of these entry points.",
      "role": "primary-authority"
    },
    {
      "anchor": {
        "blob": "7c6601ddf7269a084e197eb6ae1f071a8c3acef6",
        "content": "sha256:a4cb15f991923645d5bd6bd9654729ebd68da71c047ec096d8112ba5087c5a36",
        "locator": {
          "kind": "symbol",
          "name": "subjectSelection"
        }
      },
      "id": "RLZ-NENP96",
      "invariant": "INV-T1ZHP5",
      "origin": {
        "handoffEntry": "MIK-R39@v1-focus-request-answered-by-its-selection",
        "leaf": "260928-MIK-L39"
      },
      "rationale": "Its `selectSubject` leaves the request before it begins the selection, with the element that has focus and the number of the tree intent that is current, so only a render of this selection or a later one can take it.",
      "role": "support"
    },
    {
      "anchor": {
        "blob": "7c6601ddf7269a084e197eb6ae1f071a8c3acef6",
        "content": "sha256:ed42abbe8b4b69f82670123053f5462afd7d5f4004110fe9e68e5e351b9f61e6",
        "locator": {
          "kind": "symbol",
          "name": "useSurface"
        }
      },
      "id": "RLZ-PCQKA3",
      "invariant": "INV-9ZKYWQ",
      "origin": {
        "handoffEntry": "MIK-R39@v1-other-selections-start-afresh",
        "leaf": "260928-MIK-L39"
      },
      "rationale": "Builds the selection handlers and the refresh and retry handlers over the one workspace state and the one read cycle, and hands the failure block the retry and the offer of the task context, so every entry point of the surface goes through the handlers that set the tree intent.",
      "role": "propagation-persistence"
    },
    {
      "anchor": {
        "blob": "7c6601ddf7269a084e197eb6ae1f071a8c3acef6",
        "content": "sha256:a4bfba333df278c94115c450a4e5f448cd733666f83696b2e21e3f11659b69dd",
